cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If DiagHam contributes to your work, cite the DiagHam authors: the papers
  relevant to the methods you used from the DiagHam publication list
  (https://www.nick-ux.org/diagham/index.php/Articles; DiagHam has no single
  reference paper) and, as software, DiagHam itself at https://www.nick-ux.org/diagham/.
  This repository only adds a build system, a test suite and documentation
  to their code; do not cite it in place of DiagHam.
title: DiagHam
type: software
abstract: >-
  Exact-diagonalization toolkit for strongly correlated quantum systems:
  fractional quantum Hall effect, fractional Chern and topological
  insulators, Hubbard models, spin chains and quantum dots.
authors:
  - family-names: Regnault
    given-names: Nicolas
  - family-names: Möller
    given-names: Gunnar
  - family-names: Repellin
    given-names: Cécile
  - family-names: Sterdyniak
    given-names: Antoine
  - family-names: Papić
    given-names: Zlatko
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Duc Phuong
  - family-names: Moran
    given-names: Niall
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Yang-Le
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulWatford/diagham-cmake-poc
url: https://www.nick-ux.org/diagham/
version: 2026.9.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
# DiagHam Subversion revision carried: r4493 (scripts_cmake/upstream-revision.txt).
# No DOI is minted for this repository: DiagHam is the DiagHam authors' work, and any citable archive of it is theirs to create.
keywords:
  - exact diagonalization
  - fractional quantum Hall effect
  - fractional Chern insulators
  - Hubbard model
  - spin chains
